{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"# Evidence Integration Ledger\n\n**R01: Legal Order & Authority**\nNo evidence for legal order, recommendation, execution, check, or closure authority is present in [S03], [S04], [S05], or [S06].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind legal authority; no source-grounded basis for order issuance.\n\n**R02: Hazard Triggers & Zone Sequencing**\n[S04] notes South Pass closes under smoke visibility below 150 meters [S04]. North Bridge excludes full-size buses above 54°C [S04]. No explicit fire triggers or forecast binding found in [S03], [S04], [S05], or [S06].\n*   **Disposition:** Partial. Route constraints exist, but trigger logic is absent.\n*   **Qualifications:** Smoke and heat conditions invalidate routes post-plan.\n*   **Blockers:** Missing conservative fire/weather triggers; no expiry logic defined.\n\n**R03: Population Basis & Assistance Demand**\n[S03] specifies Zone A (5,280), B (8,940), C (12,600) residents plus up to 2,100 tourists [S03]. Survey coverage is 91% [S03]. Categories (no vehicle, mobility, oxygen, dialysis) overlap and must not be summed as independent people [S03].\n*   **Disposition:** Accepted with qualification.\n*   **Qualifications:** Must carry uncertainty allowance for unreported households; cannot treat unregistered as self-evacuating [S03]. Tourist demand is time-dependent [S03].\n*   **Blockers:** None identified in source, but overlap logic must be enforced to avoid double-counting.\n\n**R04: Road Bottlenecks & Route Clearance**\n[S04] establishes Mill Junction as the system bottleneck with a measured sustainable throughput of 1,500 vehicles/hour [S04]. North Bridge (1,100 veh/h) and South Pass (850 veh/h) feed into Mill Junction; their capacities cannot be added [S04]. Last exercise achieved only 1,180 veh/h at Mill Junction due to unmanaged lane merging [S04].\n*   **Disposition:** Accepted.\n*   **Qualifications:** Do not sum independent road ratings across the shared downstream bottleneck [S04]. Clearance time must use shared junction and exercise throughput until a current field test proves otherwise [S04].\n*   **Blockers:** Contraflow requires sheriff closure, 45 minutes setup, and staffed crossover points [S04]. County 12 cannot be fully converted to outbound traffic [S04].\n\n**R05: Fleet Matching & Driver Duty**\n[S05] details fleet availability: 18 county buses exist, but only 11 qualified drivers can report within two hours [S05]. Four lift-equipped buses carry two occupied wheelchairs and thirty-four seated riders each [S05]. Twelve school buses become available at 14:30, after student release; they cannot be assumed in an earlier Zone A clearance [S05]. Ambulances are reserved for clinical need and are not general mobility vehicles [S05]. Drivers have a twelve-hour duty ceiling; a route plan that uses every driver for outbound movement leaves no legal return, relief, or shelter-transfer capacity [S05].\n*   **Disposition:** Accepted with qualification.\n*   **Qualifications:** Nominal seats are not the same as sustained evacuation throughput due to fuel endurance and delayed resupply constraints [S05]. Cycle times range from 35m to 95m depending on vehicle type and status [S05]. Roster-gap vehicles (e.g., FLEET-000, FLEET-008) are not immediately operational without additional staffing [S05].\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind fleet requirements beyond observed driver limits and specific vehicle configurations; no cycle time data available for combined route-shelter loops.\n\n**R06: Shelter Capacity & Medical Handoffs**\n[S06] specifies four sites with 8,200 nominal spaces, but smoke-safe staffed capacity is 5,900 [S06]. Civic Arena has 48 accessible cots, Expo Hall 64, Ridge School none, and West College 32 [S06]. Expo Hall's primary route crosses the South Pass smoke corridor [S06]. Ridge School does not accept pets and lacks backup filtration [S06]. Civic Arena's generator has sixteen hours of tested fuel [S06].\n*   **Disposition:** Accepted with qualification.\n*   **Qualifications:** A shelter is usable only when staffing, filtration, backup power, sanitation, and route access are current for the same operational period; nominal floor area is not readiness [S06]. Medical accommodation and animal handling change effective capacity [S06]. Air-quality thresholds may require relocation after initial opening [S06].\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot verify shelter suitability or medical continuity without current staffing and filtration status.\n\n**R07: Warnings & Community Support**\nNo evidence for redundant multilingual warning, door-knock timing, radio interoperability, receipt/understanding evidence, or zone revision is present in [S03], [S04], [S05], or [S06].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind communication strategy.\n\n**R08: Fuel & Power Continuity**\nNo evidence for fuel/power continuity, observed delays, local staging, alternate routes/suppliers, or coupled asset effects is present in [S03], [S04], [S05], or [S06].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind resource contracting.\n\n**R09: Animals & Service Animals**\nNo evidence for animal handling or service animal separation without delaying human evacuation is present in [S03], [S04], [S05], or [S06].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind animal logistics.\n\n**R10: Accountability & Data Privacy**\nNo evidence for private accountability, public aggregation, self-evacuation tracking, restricted health data handling, reconciliation, retention, or deletion proof is present in [S03], [S04], [S05], or [S06].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind data management protocol.\n\n**R11: 48-Hour Execution Sequence**\nNo evidence for a concrete 48-hour sequence with owners, effects, current checks, repair, recheck, resource/cost authority, and contingencies is present in [S03], [S04], [S05], or [S06].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind execution timeline.\n\n**R12: Verification & Readiness Blockers**\nNo evidence for exercise blockers, independent-review blockers, candidate-bound readiness, uncertainties, or explicit falsifiers is present in [S03], [S04], [S05], or [S06].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot verify readiness status.\n\n**Cross-Source Relationships & Contradictions**\n[S03] and [S04] are complementary but disjoint: [S03] defines demand (population, assistance categories) while [S04] defines supply constraints (road throughput, junction bottlenecks). [S05] provides fleet details that must be matched to [S03] demand and constrained by [S04] bridge restrictions. [S06] provides shelter capacity that must be coupled to route and transport plans from [S04] and [S05]. No contradictions exist between these sources, but both lack evidence for legal authority (R01), communications (R07), resources (R08), animals (R09), data privacy (R10), execution sequence (R11), and verification (R12). The integration is incomplete for a full evacuation decision.\n\n**Unresolved Evidence**\n*   Specific trigger values for fire/weather (R02) are absent in [S03]/[S04].\n*   Fleet matching logic linking [S03] demand to vehicle capacity is partially present in [S05] but lacks combined route-shelter loop data.\n*   Shelter location and capacity data are present in [S06] but lack current staffing and filtration status."}}],"created":1787628973,"model":"Qwen3.8-27B-AD-IQ2_S.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10434-7e4c0a968","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":1871,"prompt_tokens":6687,"total_tokens":8558,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-Qmft5VuZr8155RPTYW8AHkOjgQ3noRYC","__verbose":{"index":0,"content":"# Evidence Integration Ledger\n\n**R01: Legal Order & Authority**\nNo evidence for legal order, recommendation, execution, check, or closure authority is present in [S03], [S04], [S05], or 